## Comparing Two AI Careers

This research compares two real job postings: AI Engineer I at American Express and AI Forward Deployed Engineer at Cognizant.

## Role 1: AI Engineer I

**Company:** American Express  
**Job Posting:** [AI Engineer I](https://egug.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/26012982)  
**Date Checked:** November 14, 2026

**Main Responsibilities:**
- Develop AI-powered software.
- Write and test Python code.
- Work with data and machine learning.
- Improve AI systems.

**Skills Requested:**
- Python programming.
- Computer science fundamentals.
- Data processing.
- Knowledge of AI and machine learning.

**Experience Level:** Early career.

**Deadline:** November 1, 2026 (passed).

## Role 2: AI Forward Deployed Engineer

**Company:** Cognizant  
**Job Posting:** [AI Forward Deployed Engineer](https://careers.cognizant.com/emea-en/jobs/00069909834/ai-forward-deployed-engineer/)  
**Date Checked:** November 14, 2026

**Main Responsibilities:**
- Develop AI solutions for clients.
- Connect AI models to software.
- Test applications.
- Understand and solve client problems.

**Skills Requested:**
- Programming.
- APIs and cloud technology.
- Docker and Kubernetes.
- Communication and problem-solving.

**Experience Level:** Experienced professional.

**Deadline:** November 30, 2026.

## Comparing the Careers

Both careers involve developing AI-powered software. However, an AI Engineer focuses more on building and improving AI systems, while a Forward Deployed Engineer also works closely with clients to create solutions for their needs.

AI Engineer appears to be the better starting point because the American Express posting is designed for early-career applicants. The Cognizant position requires at least five years of professional experience.

## Skills I Already Have

- Basic programming knowledge from computer science courses.
- Experience writing Java programs.
- Understanding of classes, methods, arrays, and object-oriented programming.
- Experience creating and testing software projects.

## Skills I Need to Improve

1. **AI and Machine Learning:** Learn how AI models work and how to use them in applications.
2. **APIs and Deployment:** Learn how applications communicate with AI services and how to make projects available online.

## One-Week Action Plan

**Day 1–2:** Research basic AI concepts and Python libraries.

**Day 3–4:** Learn how APIs connect applications to other services.

**Day 5–6:** Start a small AI-powered project.

**Day 7:** Test the project and document what I learned.

## Conclusion

My main career interest is AI Engineering because it combines programming with artificial intelligence. AI Forward Deployed Engineering is another career worth exploring in the future because it combines technical skills with communication and problem-solving.
